{"config":{"schemaVersion":1,"version":"NTE-PARTNER-1.0","resourceName":"NTEAgreementBundleV1","event":{"code":"NTE2027","name":"National Transition Event","eventDate":"2027-03-01","venue":"The Wing, Silverstone, Towcester, Northamptonshire, NN12 8TN","organiser":"Mission Motorsport / Mission Community","noticeEmail":"nte@missioncommunity.org","paperworkDeadline":""},"taxText":"No VAT will be charged.","paymentText":"The Sponsorship Fee is payable in full within 30 days of signing this Agreement and on receipt of the Organiser’s invoice.","packages":[{"name":"Headline Partner","fee":30000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Gold Partner","fee":15000,"benefits":[{"heading":"Before the event","items":[["Partnership announcement social media post","Individual post"],["Dedicated company story and social media posts","Included"],["Dedicated individual Armed Forces community member story post","Included"],["Partner logo montage on NTE website homepage with URL link","Included"],["Reserved complimentary tickets for Sunday Night Party at Escapade","6"]]},{"heading":"During the event","items":[["Exhibitor stand space included in location of choice","Very large stand"],["Thanked in speeches","Included"],["Branding placements","Gold banner in your hall"],["Partnership included in the event guide and PDF circulated to registered attendees and exhibitors before the event","Included"],["Advert in event guide","Full page"],["Team tickets to attend NTE on the stand with lunch vouchers","10"],["Event Partner Recognition Certificate for displaying on the stand","Included"],["GP circuit passenger rides for staff","10"]]},{"heading":"After the event","items":[["Post-event social media thank you","Included"],["Downloadable link to professional images and video","Included"],["Partnership remains on NTE website","10 months"],["Social Value Report on event community impact","Included"],["Armed Forces advocacy evidence for ERS awards/revalidation","Included"]]}]},{"name":"Premier Partner","fee":7000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Champion Partner","fee":2000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Zone Sponsor","fee":5000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Community Stage Sponsor","fee":6000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Podcast Corner Sponsor","fee":6000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Event Guide Sponsor","fee":5000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Delegate Tote Bag Sponsor","fee":5000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Helmet Bay Sponsor","fee":3000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Auditorium Sponsor","fee":5000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Live Stream Sponsor","fee":6000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Wristband Sponsor","fee":3000,"benefits":[]},{"name":"Escapade Sponsor","fee":9000,"benefits":[]}]},"template":"<article class=\"agreement-document\">\n<h1>{{eventName}} {{packageTitle}} Agreement</h1>\n<p><strong>Organiser:</strong> {{organiser}}</p>\n<p><strong>Sponsor:</strong> {{organisation}}<br/>{{address}}</p>\n<p><strong>Event:</strong> {{eventName}} ({{eventCode}}), {{eventDate}}<br/><strong>Venue:</strong> {{venue}}</p>\n<p>Dear {{signatory}},</p>\n<p>Thank you for your support for the Event. Without partnerships an event of this kind would not be possible.</p><p>This letter and attached Schedule sets out the terms and arrangements of sponsorship, in particular, key definitions and details (Event, Venue, Sponsorship Fee, Promotional Materials, Sponsor Branding, Promotion, Event Services, Intellectual Property Rights).</p><p>The Sponsor will provide the Organiser with financial sponsorship for the National Transition Event and the Organiser will in return appoint the Sponsor as non-exclusive sponsor and will promote the Sponsor’s name and business at the Event.</p><h2>1. The Organiser’s responsibilities</h2><p>The Organiser undertakes to:</p><p>1.1 host, organise, and run the National Transition Event and provide the Venue;</p><p>1.2 provide the Sponsor with the Promotion and the Event Services (at and in relation to the Event) as detailed in the Schedule;</p><p>1.3 prepare and provide the Promotional Materials, and use them as detailed in the Schedule;</p><p>1.4 neither make any public or other statement about the Sponsor or its business, products or services that contains negative, derogatory, or misleading content, nor use any Sponsor Branding nor any other branding nor any other item relating to the Sponsor&#39;s business without the Sponsor&#39;s prior approval (whether or not it relates to the Event), except that the Organiser may make factual statements about the Sponsor&#39;s sponsorship of the Event for legitimate promotional, marketing, or coordination purposes and may use the Sponsor Branding as permitted by Clause 2.3 below and as detailed in the Schedule;</p><p>1.5 not do anything at or in relation to the Event likely to harm the Sponsor’s business reputation or goodwill attaching to its business or Sponsor Branding; and</p><p>1.6 ensure that it complies with all legal requirements and that it has all necessary authorities, licences, and consents to run the Event, to meet its obligations under this Agreement and for the parties to implement this Agreement generally.</p><h2>2. The Sponsor’s responsibilities</h2><p>The Sponsor undertakes:</p><p>2.1 to pay the Organiser the Sponsorship Fee as set out in the Schedule;</p><p>2.2 to provide the Organiser in good time with suitable electronic copies of the Sponsor Branding to use in the Promotional Materials;</p><p>2.3 to permit the Organiser to use the Sponsor Branding as necessary to enable the Organiser to provide the Sponsor Promotion and Event Services to host, organise, and run the Event, but does not grant the Organiser any other right or licence under the Sponsor’s Intellectual Property Rights;</p><p>2.4 that the Sponsor Branding does not and will not infringe any Intellectual Property Rights of any third party, and the Sponsor will indemnify and hold harmless the Organiser against any claims, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from any third-party infringement claims related to the Organiser&#39;s use of the Sponsor Branding in accordance with this Agreement; and</p><p>2.5 to advertise or make any public statements about the Sponsor’s sponsorship of the Event only if such statements do not contain any negative comment about the Organiser or the Event.</p><h2>3. Circumstances beyond the reasonable control of either party</h2><p>If the Organiser or the Sponsor (“party”) fails to perform or delays in performing any obligation due to circumstance beyond that party’s reasonable control (“Force Majeure”), that party shall not be considered to be in breach of or liable for that failure or delay.</p><h2>4. Termination</h2><h3>4.1 For force majeure</h3><p>4.1.1 Where there is Force Majeure and as a result it reasonably appears to either party at any time that the Event cannot commence, or cannot continue until its conclusion as or when contemplated by this Agreement, either party may promptly at that time terminate this Agreement by notice to the other party.</p><p>4.1.2 If, at the time of serving that notice, any two or more of the promotional activities specified in clause 4.1.2.2 below have not been completed:</p><p>4.1.2.1 either  (a) the Event has not commenced; or (b) the Event has commenced, but fewer than two of the promotional activities specified in clause 4.1.2.2 below have been completed - none of the Sponsorship Fee shall be payable, and if any has been paid it shall be promptly returned to the Sponsor; or</p><p>4.1.2.2 the Event has commenced and any two or more of the following promotional activities have been completed: (i) social media posts featuring the Sponsor&#39;s branding have been published, (ii) the Sponsor&#39;s logo has been displayed on the event website for at least 7 days, (iii) promotional materials containing the Sponsor&#39;s branding have been distributed, or (iv) the Event has run for at least 25% of its scheduled duration, then 50% of the Sponsorship Fee shall be and remain payable, and any sum previously paid over and above 50% shall be promptly returned to the Sponsor.</p><h3>4.2 For no good reason</h3><p>If the Organiser cancels the Event at a time when there is no Force Majeure and there is no breach of this Agreement by the Sponsor, the Organiser may do so by notice to the Sponsor. In such circumstances: (a) if cancellation occurs more than 60 days before the Event, the Organiser may retain up to 25% of the Sponsorship Fee to cover reasonable costs incurred, with the remainder promptly returned to the Sponsor; (b) if cancellation occurs 60 days or fewer before the Event, the Organiser may retain up to 50% of the Sponsorship Fee to cover reasonable costs incurred, with the remainder promptly returned to the Sponsor.</p><h3>4.3 For breach</h3><p>Either party may terminate this Agreement by giving notice to the other if the other commits any breach of a material obligation under this Agreement (including failure to pay any sum due) and fails to remedy it within 30 days after being given notice containing details of the breach and requiring it to be remedied. Upon such termination, if the party in breach is:</p><p>4.3.1 The Organiser, it may not retain or receive any Sponsorship Fee, and it must promptly return any of it previously paid; or</p><p>4.3.2    the Sponsor, the Organiser will be entitled to receive and retain a proportion of the Sponsorship Fee corresponding to the promotional activities and Event Services already provided or committed to at the time of breach, with any excess amount to be promptly returned to the Sponsor.</p><h2>5. Confidentiality</h2><p>Except as the parties may otherwise agree in relation to any particular information, each party undertakes to the other to keep confidential all confidential information of the other, to use it only if and to the extent necessary to carry out this Agreement, and not disclose any such confidential information to any third party. This undertaking shall not apply to any information which: (a) is in the public domain otherwise than due to a breach of this undertaking; (b) is required to be disclosed by law, regulation, or court order; (c) is necessary for event promotion, marketing, or coordination activities contemplated by this Agreement; (d) is disclosed to professional advisers, auditors, or other service providers under appropriate confidentiality obligations; or (e) relates to the existence and general terms of this sponsorship arrangement for legitimate business purposes including coordination with other event participants.</p><h2>6. Data protection</h2><p>Each party shall comply with all its respective obligations under the Data Protection Act 2018 and any other applicable or equivalent data protection or privacy legislation, regulations or guidance from time to time relating to the processing of personal data.</p><h2>7. Notices</h2><p>Any notice to be given under this Agreement by either party to the other shall be in writing, signed by or on behalf of whoever gives the notice, and sent by email as follows:</p><p>7.1 To the Sponsor: {{email}}</p><p>7.2 To the Organiser: {{noticeEmail}}</p><h2>8. General</h2><p>8.1 This Agreement shall constitute only the contractual relationship provided for in this Agreement and neither party shall be a partner, agent, employee, or joint venturer of the other.</p><p>8.2 This Agreement is personal to each of the parties, and no obligation or rights under it may be assigned, sub-contracted, sub-licenced or otherwise delegated except as the parties may agree in writing.</p><p>8.3 Except as set out in this Agreement, the parties have not agreed any other terms, responsibilities, rights, or other details in relation to the Event or the Promotion, nor will either party rely on any statements or promises made to it by the other unless they are set out in this Agreement.</p><p>This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales.</p><p>Each party irrevocably agrees that the courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with this Agreement or its subject matter or formation (including non-contractual disputes or claims).</p><p>If you have any questions or wish to propose an amendment to this Agreement please do not sign, but instead get in touch, and we can agree a revised document for you to sign.</p>\n<h2>Schedule</h2>\n<p>“The Event” means the {{eventName}} taking place on {{eventDate}}. “The Venue” means {{venue}}.</p>\n<p>“Event Services” means the package services set out below.</p>\n{{packages}}\n<p><strong>The Sponsorship Fee: {{fee}}</strong> {{taxText}} {{paymentText}}</p>\n{{deadline}}\n<p>“The Sponsor Branding” means Sponsor logo, trade or service marks, other marketing signs, and any accompanying artwork, design or slogans.</p><p>“Intellectual Property Rights” means all intellectual property rights in the Sponsor Branding belonging to the Sponsor, including, for example, copyright, trade/service marks (registered or unregistered), rights to sue for passing off, domain names, goodwill, or rights in confidential information. Other terms, are defined in the Schedule.</p>\n<div class=\"signature-block\"><h2>Signed for and on behalf of {{organisation}}</h2>\n<p>The Partner Sponsor agrees to the terms of this agreement and its Schedule.</p>\n{{signature}}\n<p><strong>Signatory:</strong> {{signatory}}<br/><strong>Email:</strong> {{email}}<br/><strong>Signed:</strong> {{signedAt}}</p>\n<p><strong>Authority confirmed:</strong> Yes<br/><strong>Agreement accepted:</strong> Yes</p>\n</div>\n<p class=\"audit\"><strong>Agreement version:</strong> {{version}}<br/><strong>Reference:</strong> {{reference}}{{evidence}}</p>\n</article>"}